2 specialisations / talent trees: Beast Hunter & Survival Hunter


Beast Hunter overview:
- pet companion
- focus on using your pet as health and damage
- own attacks are almost entirely ranged 
- good at control/manipulation over a single enemy
- relies on keeping distance from the enemy as much as possible 


Survival Hunter overview:
- high visibility (larger field of view)
- mix of ranged attacks and melee attacks
- often utilises traps
- most comfortable fighting at a distance, but able to hold their own up-close

Beast Hunter basic abilities:
- Pet Charge: cause your pet to continually run towards the nearest enemy while attacking them
- Pet Heal: heal your pet, and temporarily boost defence
- Force Shot: shoot at a distance and push the enemy backwards and slow them slightly
- Throw: throw one adjacent target away from you (enemies and allies can be thrown)

Survival Hunter basic abilities:
- Damage Trap: place a damaging trap that is only visible when very close
- Tracking Shot: a shot that curves towards the first enemy it sees (curve not so good that it always hits, but slightly-off aim should hit, and enemy running straight away will be bad)
- Axe Swipe: swipe your axe causing moderately high melee damage
- Throw Mud: throw mud in the eyes of a nearby enemy reducing maximum field-of-view for 10s (and does a small amount of damage)


Hunter basic abilities (shared):
- Wide Eyed: increase field of view for 30s
- Long Shot: a shot that can fire a long distance quite accurately (precisely where the player aims, not necessarily at a target)